    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1162">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1144" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1144"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Loomis.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 156.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 156, of the 19th ultimo, inclosing the records in the case of Felipe
                    Scandella, an American citizen, expelled from Venezuela by the authorities of
                    Ciudad Bolivar.</p>
                <p>The Department appreciates the successful manner in which you conducted the case,
                    which you were instructed to settle in accordance with the Department’s telegram
                    of the 30th ultimo.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
